WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.552 --> 00:00:17.179
The crackling from the fireplace gave the impression that all was well in the March home.

2
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.962
Another crackling sound, that of Jo pushing down on her knuckles, told a different story.

3
00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:28.244
"I wish this bothersome snow would stop."

4
00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:34.966
Jo banged the window as she watched the gigantic snowflakes silently piling up on the ground.

5
00:00:34.986 --> 00:00:40.447
"Jo," shrieked Amy, "that's so unladylike!"

6
00:00:41.547 --> 00:00:44.328
Amy smoothed her dress and caressed her curls.

7
00:00:45.288 --> 00:00:48.849
She could not stand it when her older sister acted like a boy.

8
00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.830
Jo, on the other hand, wished she could be a boy.

9
00:00:54.291 --> 00:00:58.192
She often complained: "Why do I have to wear this confining dress?

10
00:00:59.112 --> 00:01:03.715
Why can't I wear trousers and kick my legs up and gallop around freely, like a horse?"

11
00:01:05.156 --> 00:01:13.002
Whenever Jo said such things, her older sister Meg would gently shake her head and say: "Because whether

12
00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:15.123
you like it or not, you are a girl.

13
00:01:16.004 --> 00:01:17.745
And girls should behave as such."

14
00:01:18.706 --> 00:01:23.249
On this cold winter day, however, Meg did not scold her tomboy sister.

15
00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:27.892
In fact, she agreed with Jo about the endlessly falling snow.

16
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:32.393
"It's so cold and miserable," Meg lamented.

17
00:01:32.413 --> 00:01:36.694
"When we were rich, we could warm up every room in the house."

18
00:01:37.674 --> 00:01:41.395
Now the only room that was heated was the living room in which they sat.

19
00:01:42.436 --> 00:01:45.677
"We didn't have to wear these unbecoming sweaters."

20
00:01:46.637 --> 00:01:50.058
Amy turned up her nose as if her sweater had a funny smell.

21
00:01:50.078 --> 00:01:58.224
"Now our concerns are about how Father is faring under these treacherous conditions," added Jo.

22
00:01:58.244 --> 00:02:02.685
She stomped over to the fireplace and rubbed her large hands together vigorously.

23
00:02:03.946 --> 00:02:09.547
Being over the age at which men could enlist in the army, Father had volunteered his services as

24
00:02:09.607 --> 00:02:10.207
a clergyman.

25
00:02:11.268 --> 00:02:15.489
The girls were too young to understand or to care what the Civil War was about.

26
00:02:17.049 --> 00:02:20.190
They only wanted it to end so Father could return home.

27
00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.971
At one time, the March family had been very wealthy.

28
00:02:25.031 --> 00:02:30.334
Meg and Jo, the two oldest girls, could remember a time when they received many gifts all year

29
00:02:30.354 --> 00:02:35.577
around. Now they didn't have enough money to buy even Christmas gifts for each other.

30
00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:40.039
"If you had five dollars Jo began.

31
00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:44.162
(At this period of time, five dollars was a lot of money.)

32
00:02:45.282 --> 00:02:49.625
"If you had five dollars," Jo repeated, "what would you buy?"

33
00:02:50.746 --> 00:02:54.648
The girls fell silent as their eyes grew bigger with fanciful thoughts.

34
00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:58.802
"I know what I would buy," Amy gushed at last.

35
00:02:59.602 --> 00:03:00.743
Her sisters turned to her.

36
00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:03.184
"Go on," urged Jo.

37
00:03:04.865 --> 00:03:08.927
Amy's cheeks got pink and she pressed her hands together excitedly.

38
00:03:10.128 --> 00:03:13.170
"I would buy a new set of watercolors," she said.

39
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:20.394
"And then I would buy two new hairpins: one red with silver butterflies, like my best friend Kitty

40
00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:24.036
has. And the other blue like my eyes."

41
00:03:25.668 --> 00:03:31.191
"As for me," Meg said, "I would buy beautiful silk material for a new dress.

42
00:03:32.092 --> 00:03:36.835
Maybe I would have some money left over for gloves since I desperately need new ones."

43
00:03:37.855 --> 00:03:42.038
Meg held up her lovely hands, which were now pinkish red from the cold.

44
00:03:43.118 --> 00:03:49.602
Meg had many vanities but she took special pride in her hands.

45
00:03:49.622 --> 00:03:56.239
"I," Jo blurted in a loud, comical voice, "would buy four bottles of black ink, a case of

46
00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:02.305
pens, twenty rolls of paper, and three hundred she paused for dramatic emphasis.

47
00:04:03.566 --> 00:04:09.852
"Three hundred," she repeated again, "leather cases for all the books I am going to publish."

48
00:04:10.893 --> 00:04:12.654
Jo dreamed of being a writer.

49
00:04:13.655 --> 00:04:18.660
Nothing suited her more than to sit at her desk and enter a world of make-believe and fantasy.

50
00:04:20.148 --> 00:04:23.829
"You can't afford that many leather cases with only five dollars.

51
00:04:24.729 --> 00:04:27.090
That's ridiculous," Amy pointed out.

52
00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:33.972
"Well, so is this game," Jo retorted, "because none of us actually has five dollars!"

53
00:04:33.992 --> 00:04:37.853
"Girls," Meg said in her "motherly" voice.

54
00:04:37.873 --> 00:04:39.714
"Do stop arguing.

55
00:04:40.074 --> 00:04:41.634
You're behaving like children.

56
00:04:42.895 --> 00:04:46.456
Now, Beth, let's hear what you would do if you had five dollars."

57
00:04:48.384 --> 00:04:50.705
Beth had a faraway look in her eyes.

58
00:04:51.066 --> 00:04:51.766
She was smiling.

59
00:04:51.786 --> 00:04:57.109
"First of all, I'd buy a new pair of slippers for Mother.

60
00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:04.173
I noticed her old ones have several small holes in them," Beth said in her gentle, quiet way.

61
00:05:05.213 --> 00:05:08.595
The other girls glanced at the familiar slippers next to the sofa.

62
00:05:09.356 --> 00:05:14.739
They all felt rather guilty when they saw that the well-worn slippers did, indeed, have many holes.

63
00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:21.723
"And then I would buy Father a new scarf and hat in his favorite color," Beth continued.

64
00:05:21.743 --> 00:05:27.946
"If I had money left over, I would get each of you girls a handkerchief with your name

65
00:05:28.086 --> 00:05:28.347
on it.

66
00:05:29.027 --> 00:05:30.528
And one for Hannah, too."

67
00:05:31.709 --> 00:05:35.931
Of the four girls, Beth was by far the kindest and most loving.

68
00:05:36.872 --> 00:05:40.394
She never said a bad word about anyone nor did she ever complain.

69
00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:44.156
She had a positive view of everything and everyone.

70
00:05:45.612 --> 00:05:46.393
"Oh, Beth!"

71
00:05:46.693 --> 00:05:49.175
Jo ran over and wrapped her arms around her sister.

72
00:05:49.195 --> 00:05:52.057
"You make me feel so ashamed!

73
00:05:52.838 --> 00:06:00.764
Here I am thinking of myself, but you—" she sniffed, for Jo was a very emotional girl, "—you

74
00:06:00.844 --> 00:06:03.306
even thought of Hannah, our housekeeper."

75
00:06:04.587 --> 00:06:06.688
Meg and Amy also gave Beth a hug.

76
00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:11.232
They, too, were feeling a little embarrassed about their selfishness.

77
00:06:13.136 --> 00:06:18.579
Even though the sisters had different personalities, they were very close and loved one another very much.

78
00:06:18.599 --> 00:06:21.301
"Girls, what is going on?"

79
00:06:22.441 --> 00:06:24.382
The girls had not heard Mother come home.

80
00:06:24.402 --> 00:06:28.945
"Mother!" they cried and ran to give her a hug.

81
00:06:29.925 --> 00:06:35.348
Mother's hands and cheeks were cold from the air outside, but her hugs and kisses warmed the girls

82
00:06:35.428 --> 00:06:36.148
up instantly.

83
00:06:37.309 --> 00:06:39.310
Meg quickly removed Mother's heavy coat.

84
00:06:40.511 --> 00:06:42.492
Jo ran to get more wood for the fire.

85
00:06:43.684 --> 00:06:48.066
Amy grabbed Mother's sweater, which was folded up on her chair, and gave it to her.

86
00:06:49.086 --> 00:06:51.948
Beth quietly brought Mother's slippers to warm her feet.

87
00:06:53.028 --> 00:06:57.530
As Mother sat on her chair and rubbed her hands in front of the fire, Jo told her

88
00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:58.851
what they'd been talking about.

89
00:06:58.871 --> 00:07:03.133
"We were so selfish, Mother," admitted Jo.

90
00:07:03.153 --> 00:07:04.673
"Except for Beth.

91
00:07:05.073 --> 00:07:06.934
She only cares about other people."

92
00:07:08.215 --> 00:07:13.933
Mother smiled affectionately at each daughter and said: "I'm glad that you discovered your fault, girls.

93
00:07:14.873 --> 00:07:17.734
But finding out our faults is only the first step.

94
00:07:18.834 --> 00:07:21.515
What we do with this knowledge is more important."

95
00:07:23.355 --> 00:07:29.137
That evening, after a simple dinner, Mother and Hannah took inventory of the food pantry while the girls

96
00:07:29.177 --> 00:07:31.117
sat around the fireplace talking again.

97
00:07:31.137 --> 00:07:34.818
"I have some money saved up," Jo began.

98
00:07:34.838 --> 00:07:43.150
"It's only a little bit but, well, I wanted Mother a little gift she stammered.

99
00:07:44.371 --> 00:07:45.091
"Oh, Jo!

100
00:07:45.812 --> 00:07:47.073
What a lovely thought!"

101
00:07:47.853 --> 00:07:51.436
Beth understood right away what her sister was trying hard to express.

102
00:07:51.456 --> 00:07:54.818
"What's a lovely thought?"

103
00:07:55.319 --> 00:07:56.339
Amy asked irritably.

104
00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:00.342
Unlike Beth, she had no idea what Jo was trying to say.

105
00:08:00.362 --> 00:08:05.106
"This Christmas none of us has much to give," Beth explained.

106
00:08:05.126 --> 00:08:10.902
"But with what we do have, Jo suggests that we should all give something to Mother."

107
00:08:11.863 --> 00:08:14.645
Beth smiled at Jo, who nodded enthusiastically.

108
00:08:14.665 --> 00:08:19.709
"That's exactly what I wanted to say, Beth," she said gratefully.

109
00:08:20.729 --> 00:08:23.451
Meg and Amy both agreed it was a splendid idea.

110
00:08:24.532 --> 00:08:28.855
They spent the rest of the evening discussing what Mother needed and what they could give her.

111
00:08:30.056 --> 00:08:35.060
Although the girls would not receive gifts themselves, they were quite happy to learn the true meaning of

112
00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:35.400
giving.
